<title>UK: General Cable buys Imminus.</title>
<headline>General Cable buys Imminus.</headline>
<dateline>LONDON 1997-03-13</dateline>
<text>
<p>British cable communications supplier General Cable Plc said on Thursday it had bought British managed data network services Imminus Ltd for a maxium 33 million stg.</p>
<p>General Cable said 19.5 million stg would be payable in cash and 7.1 million in loan notes. Up to a further 6.4 million stg would be payable to Imminus management shareholders one and two years after the acqusition. The remainging sum would be paid in cash or in General Cable shares.  </p>
<p>General Cable said the acquisition would enable it to exploit the growing market in switched data services. It said Imminus was particularly active in the travel market.</p>
<p>--London Newsroom +44 171 542 4017</p>
